     "content": "This is a **very strong offer**, and Google made a substantial concession by offering a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** to eliminate your switching risk. \n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\nWith the updated base ($240k), bonus target ($48k), $1.08M stock (front-loaded 33/33/22/12), and $200k cash sign-on:\n\n| Component | Year 1 (Google) | Year 2 (Google) | Year 3 (Google) | Meta (Current / yr) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Bonus (Target)** | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 (20%) | ~$36,000 (15%) |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | **$200,000** | $0 | $0 | $0 |\n| **Equity Vesting** | $356,400 (33%) | $356,400 (33%) | $237,600 (22%) | ~$250,000 |\n| **Refreshes** | $0 | Refreshes start | + Refreshes | + Meta Refreshes |\n| **Total Comp (TC)** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,400** | **~$525,600 + refreshes** | **~$526,000** |\n\n#### The 2-Year Reality:\n* **Google (Years 1 & 2 combined):** **~$1,488,800**\n* **Meta (Years 1 & 2 combined):** **~$1,052,000**\n* **Net Surplus:** You will make roughly **+$436,800 more in liquid compensation over the next 24 months** by moving to Google.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is an Exceptional Google L6 Offer\n* **Sign-on Bonus:** A $200,000 upfront cash sign-on at Google is at the top of their discretionary limits for an L6.\n* **Base Salary Matched:** They eliminated the base-salary pay cut.\n* **Front-Loaded Liquidity:** Google's 33/33/22/12 vesting structure combined with the upfront bonus locks in a massive Year 1 payday ($844k) without you having to wait for year-end vesting cliffs.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Details to Check Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-on Bonus Clawback Terms:**\n   * Most Google sign-ons are paid in your first or second paycheck and have a **12-month clawback** (if you voluntarily leave within 12 months, you pay it back prorated or in full). Verify the timeline and whether it\u2019s a lump sum or split over two installments.\n2. **Level Mapping Reality:**\n   * Meta **IC6** is considered \"Lead / Staff PM.\" \n   * Google **L6** is titled \"Senior PM\" (Google L7 is \"Group PM / Staff PM\"). \n   * It is very common for Meta IC6s to enter Google as L6 due to strict PM leveling guidelines. However, make sure you are comfortable with the scope and reporting structure of the specific team you're joining.\n3. **The Year 3/4 Horizon:**\n   * Because of Google's front-loaded vesting (dropping from 33% to 22% in Year 3), your compensation would naturally dip in Year 3 unless sustained by annual refresh grants. Google's annual equity refreshers for strong-performing L6s help smooth this out, but you will need to perform well to keep TC above $600k in Years 3 and 4.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Recommendation\n\n**You should accept the offer.**\n\nYou stated that compensation matters a lot to you. Securing an extra **~$435,000 over two years** while matching your base and diversifying your resume across two of Big Tech's strongest PM brands is about as good of an outcome as you can achieve from an unsolicited outreach. \n\nThe recruiter has exhausted their discretionary budget (a $200k sign-on confirms they went to executive/comp committee approval for you). Pushing further risks souring the relationship; taking the win here is the right financial and career move.",
